================================================================================
ATTRIBUTION REQUIREMENTS FOR APPS THAT USE THIS SDK
================================================================================

Apps that ship this SDK distribute MapLibre Native in binary form. To comply:

1. License notice (required by the BSD 2-Clause License of both MapLibre Native
   and this SDK). Reproduce both copyright notices and license texts above in
   your app's documentation or other materials, for example an "Open source
   licenses" or "Acknowledgements" screen. Also include the notices of the
   third-party components bundled with MapLibre Native.

2. Map data attribution (required by most tile and data providers, not by
   MapLibre). The map style you load decides which data you display, and the
   data provider's terms decide what attribution you must show. For example,
   OpenStreetMap-based data requires "© OpenStreetMap contributors". The SDK
   always keeps MapLibre's attribution control visible (API_SPEC.md §5.5) so
   that the style's attribution text stays reachable. Do not hide or cover it.

3. MapLibre logo. The MapLibre license does not require you to show the logo.
   The SDK keeps it visible by default in v1.

This section is guidance, not legal advice. Check the terms of every style,
tile, and data provider you use.
